  <name>Mouse Config</name>
  <summary>Configure gaming mice on Linux</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      A desktop application for configuring gaming mice on Linux. Supports
      DPI adjustment, RGB lighting, polling rate, button remapping, macro
      recording, and battery monitoring.
    </p>
    <p>Compatible with Attack Shark, Compx, Xenta, and OEM gaming mice.</p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>DPI adjustment (50–22000, up to 6 stages)</li>
      <li>RGB lighting with multiple effects and color palettes</li>
      <li>Polling rate selection (125Hz–1000Hz)</li>
      <li>Button remapping</li>
      <li>Battery level monitoring (wireless models)</li>
      <li>Dark gamer-themed interface</li>
      <li>Automatic device detection</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  <categories>
    <category>Utility</category>
  </categories>
